{"id":185,"name":"sudowoodo","speciesId":185,"dex":185,"form":"normal","generation":2,"types":["rock"],"stats":{"hp":70,"attack":100,"defense":115,"special-attack":30,"special-defense":65,"speed":30},"abilities":[{"name":"sturdy","hidden":false},{"name":"rock-head","hidden":false},{"name":"rattled","hidden":true}],"height":12,"weight":380,"baseExp":144,"sprites":{"normal":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/185.png","shiny":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/shiny/185.png","icon":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/185.png"},"cry":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/cries/main/cries/pokemon/latest/185.ogg","genus":"Imitation Pokémon","flavor":[{"version":"gold","text":"Although it always pretends to be a tree, its composi­ tion appears to be closer to a rock than a plant."},{"version":"silver","text":"It disguises it­ self as a tree to avoid attack. It hates water, so it will disappear if it starts raining."},{"version":"crystal","text":"If a tree branch shakes when there is no wind, it's a SUDOWOODO, not a tree. It hides from the rain."},{"version":"ruby","text":"SUDOWOODO camouflages itself as a tree to avoid being attacked by enemies. However, because the forelegs remain green throughout the year, the POKéMON is easily identified as a fake during the winter."},{"version":"emerald","text":"It mimics a tree to avoid being attacked by enemies. But since its forelegs remain green throughout the year, it is easily identified as a fake in the winter."},{"version":"firered","text":"It disguises itself as a tree to avoid attack. It hates water, so it will disappear if it starts raining."},{"version":"leafgreen","text":"Although it always pretends to be a tree, its composition appears to be closer to a rock than a plant."},{"version":"diamond","text":"Despite appearing to be a tree, its body is closer to rocks and stones. It is very weak to water."},{"version":"pearl","text":"It stands along paths pretending to be a tree. If it starts raining, it seems to disappear."},{"version":"platinum","text":"To avoid being attacked, it does nothing but mimic a tree. It hates water and flees from rain."},{"version":"heartgold","text":"Although it always pretends to be a tree, its composition appears more similar to rock than to vegetation."},{"version":"omega-ruby","text":"Sudowoodo camouflages itself as a tree to avoid being attacked by enemies. However, because its hands remain green throughout the year, the Pokémon is easily identified as a fake during the winter."},{"version":"sun","text":"To avoid attack, it mimics a tree. It will run off if splashed with water, which it hates."},{"version":"moon","text":"Apparently, the larger the green parts of this Pokémon, the more collectors value it. It’s a particular favorite among elderly people."},{"version":"ultra-sun","text":"It’s so popular with the elderly that there’s a magazine devoted to this Pokémon. Fans obsess over the particular length and angle of its arms."},{"version":"ultra-moon","text":"The result of its holding the same pose all the time is arms that have become supple yet strong."},{"version":"sword","text":"If a tree branch shakes when there is no wind, it’s a Sudowoodo, not a tree. It hides from the rain."},{"version":"legends-arceus","text":"Though it pretends to be a tree, it fails to fool even children. To the touch, its body feels more like rock than tree bark. Sudowoodo's extreme aversion to water merits special note."}],"genderRate":4,"captureRate":65,"eggGroups":["mineral"],"isLegendary":false,"isMythical":false,"evolution":{"species":"bonsly","speciesId":438,"evolvesTo":[{"conditions":["Sabendo Mimic"],"species":"sudowoodo","speciesId":185,"evolvesTo":[]}]},"varieties":[{"id":185,"name":"sudowoodo","form":"normal","sprite":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/off